NOTES:
Fleet Ops Copilot 0.1.0 installed in fleetops-system.

Workloads: fleetops-mcp (Service fleetops-mcp:8080), fleetops-approvals, fleetops-agent (Service fleetops-agent:8090).
Web UI (no login, ClusterIP only, never exposed by an Ingress). It cannot decide; requests filed
from it record the typed name as unverified:<name> and can be rejected but never approved:
  kubectl --context <context> -n fleetops-system port-forward svc/fleetops-agent 8090:8090
  then open http://127.0.0.1:8090/
fleetops-agent does not start until Secret fleet-ops-copilot-claude (key ANTHROPIC_API_KEY) exists in fleetops-system.
Swarmada namespaces: warehouse-a
Model profile: cloud (claude-sonnet-5-5); API key reference: Secret fleet-ops-copilot-claude, key ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
Tracing: in-cluster backend (OpenTelemetry Collector -> Jaeger, in-memory store). Read traces with:
  kubectl --context <context> -n fleetops-system port-forward svc/fleetops-jaeger 16686:16686
  then open http://127.0.0.1:16686/.
NetworkPolicy: disabled.

Drafts are refused (DENY_DRAFT_GATE_ABSENT) unless Swarmada's FleetTask
admission webhook is served. Bind ClusterRole fleetops:approver to the people
who decide requests. See docs/RUNBOOK.md.

